    }
  }
]

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "heightFraction": 0.72
}

NOTES: Use an OrthographicCamera in a standard isometric pose for the axonometric look; keep orbit limited so the figure stays readable. Box edges: THREE.LineSegments from an EdgesGeometry of a BoxGeometry(4,8,4) with LineBasicMaterial black. Interior planes: PlaneGeometry(4,4) rotated -PI/2 about X, MeshBasicMaterial with transparent:true, depthWrite:false, side:DoubleSide, plus a matching LineLoop outline; render planes after the wireframe with sorted transparency so overlaps darken naturally. Dotted curves: build a CatmullRomCurve3 per point through its per-layer (x,y,z) samples, then either LineDashedMaterial (call computeLineDistances) with small dashSize/gapSize, or instanced small spheres along the curve for crisp dots at any zoom. Arrowheads as small ConeGeometry oriented by the curve tangent at the end parameter. Side arrows as thin cylinders + cone caps, or simply Line2 plus cone. Labels as CSS2DRenderer/HTML overlays anchored to world positions, with the two side labels CSS-rotated 90°; keep them screen-facing so they stay legible under orbit. Animate the flow by advancing a t parameter and moving five marker spheres along the curves, reversing t direction with the toggle. The layerStep state drives both plane emphasis (material opacity/color tween) and marker y-position via a short eased tween, not a hard cut.

